## v0.17 direct tooling dependencies

LazyTrae v0.17.0 provisions the following direct, pinned optional
tooling dependencies into package-owned roots only. Their lockfiles are the
source of the exact resolved versions; this list records attribution and does
not make any upstream tool an operational dependency of LazyCodex or omo.

- [Ajv](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv) 8.20.0 — MIT.
- [ast-grep](https://github.com/ast-grep/ast-grep) CLI 0.44.1 — MIT.
- [VS Code ripgrep](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-ripgrep) 1.18.0 — MIT.
- [CodeGraph](https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph) 1.4.1, including its
  platform-specific optional bundles — MIT.
- [TypeScript](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript) 5.9.3 — Apache-2.0.
- [TypeScript Language Server](https://github.com/typescript-language-server/typescript-language-server)
  5.3.0 — Apache-2.0.
- [basedpyright](https://github.com/detachhead/basedpyright) 1.39.9 — MIT.

These dependencies are installed only when the corresponding optional
LazyTrae tooling command provisions an explicit, receipt-owned root. Their
own package license files remain with their installed distributions. See the
package lockfiles under `lazytrae-plugin/packages/cli/` for checksums and
complete transitive dependency records.

